  {
   "n": 2,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Consider statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Complemented lattice is a proper subset of bounded lattice.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : A bounded and complemented lattice may or may not be a distributive lattice.<br />\nWhich of the following is/are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; A lattice is bounded iff the lattice has a greatest and a least element.<br />\n&there4; A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n&bull; Complemented lattice is defined only for bounded lattice. A bounded lattice is complemented<br />\niff atleast one complement of every element exist in lattice. An element should one or more complements.<br />\n&bull; A complemented lattice is distributive iff every element has a unique complement.</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\nLet G be a connected undirected graph of order <em>n</em> where <em>n</em> ≥ 3.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : If d(V) ≥<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9b3047b1bcd987d5037.png\" /> for each vertex <em>V</em> in <em>G</em>, then <em>G</em> is Hamiltonian. [<em>d</em>(<em>V</em>) is the degree of a vertex <em>V</em>]<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : If every vertex in <em>G </em>has even degree then <em>G</em> is Eulerian.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Neither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(c)<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is true.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is true since it is given that <em>G</em> is connected graph.</p>"
  },
  {
