  {
   "n": 5,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following Hasse diagrams:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21fc57e3071b2cb25808.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following represent a distributive lattice?</div>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "(i) and (iv) only"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "(i) and (ii) only"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "(ii) only"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "(i), (ii) and (iii) only"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(b)<br />\nHasse diagram (iii) is not lattice so can not be distributive lattice.<br />\nHasse diagram (iv) is well known non-distributive lattice since element <em>b</em> has two complements&nbsp;<em>c</em>, <em>f</em>.<br />\nHasse diagram (i) and (ii) are distributive lattice because they don&rsquo;t constant kite and pentagon structure.</p>"
  },
