  {
   "n": 9,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following is true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "If a graph is connected, then its complement must be disconnected."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Chromatic number of complete graph with <em>n</em> vertices is <em>n</em> – 1."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "If two graph <em>G</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>G</em><sub>2</sub> are isomorphic, then their complements may or may not be isomorphic."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "If any simple graph with n nodes with <em>n</em> > 1, there are atleast two vertices of same degree."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; If a graph is connected, then its complement may or may not be disconnected.<br />\n<strong>Example:</strong> cyclic graph on 5 vertices.<br />\n&bull; Chromatic number of complete graph with n vertices is n.<br />\n&bull; If two graph <em>G</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>G</em><sub>2</sub> are isomorphic, then their complements always isomorphic.<br />\n&bull; If any simple graph with n nodes with nodes &gt; 1, there are atleast two vertices of same degree.</p>"
  },
